MPV(1)                            multimedia                            MPV(1)

NNAAMMEE
       mpv - a media player

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       mmppvv [options] [file|URL|PLAYLIST|-]
       mmppvv [options] files


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       mmppvv is a media player based on MPlayer and mplayer2. It supports a wide
       variety of video file formats, audio and video codecs, and subtitle
       types. Special input URL types are available to read input from a
       variety of sources other than disk files. Depending on platform, a
       variety of different video and audio output methods are supported.

       Usage examples to get you started quickly can be found at the end of
       this man page.

IINNTTEERRAACCTTIIVVEE CCOONNTTRROOLL
       mpv has a fully configurable, command-driven control layer which allows
       you to control mpv using keyboard, mouse, or remote control (there is
       no LIRC support - configure remotes as input devices instead).

       See the ----iinnppuutt-- options for ways to customize it.

       The following listings are not necessarily complete. See eettcc//iinnppuutt..ccoonnff
       in the mpv source files for a list of default bindings. User iinnppuutt..ccoonnff
       files and Lua scripts can define additional key bindings.

       See COMMAND INTERFACE and Key names sections for more details on
       configuring keybindings.

       See also ----iinnppuutt--tteesstt for interactive binding details by key, and the
       stats built-in script for key bindings list (including print to
       terminal). By default, the ? key toggles the display of this list.

   KKeeyybbooaarrdd CCoonnttrrooll

       LLEEFFTT aanndd RRIIGGHHTT
              Seek backward/forward 5 seconds. Shift+arrow does a 1 second
              exact seek (see ----hhrr--sseeeekk).

       UUPP aanndd DDOOWWNN
              Seek forward/backward 1 minute. Shift+arrow does a 5 second
              exact seek (see ----hhrr--sseeeekk).

       CCttrrll++LLEEFFTT aanndd CCttrrll++RRIIGGHHTT
              Seek to the previous/next subtitle. Subject to some restrictions
              and might not always work; see ssuubb--sseeeekk command.

       CCttrrll++SShhiifftt++LLEEFFTT aanndd CCttrrll++SShhiifftt++RRIIGGHHTT
              Adjust subtitle delay so that the previous or next subtitle is
              displayed now. This is especially useful to sync subtitles to
              audio.

       [[ aanndd ]]
              Decrease/increase current playback speed by 10%.

       {{ aanndd }}
              Halve/double current playback speed.

       BBAACCKKSSPPAACCEE
              Reset playback speed to normal.

       SShhiifftt++BBAACCKKSSPPAACCEE
              Undo the last seek. This works only if the playlist entry was
              not changed.  Hitting it a second time will go back to the
              original position.  See rreevveerrtt--sseeeekk command for details.

       SShhiifftt++CCttrrll++BBAACCKKSSPPAACCEE
              Mark the current position. This will then be used by
              SShhiifftt++BBAACCKKSSPPAACCEE as revert position (once you seek back, the
              marker will be reset). You can use this to seek around in the
              file and then return to the exact position where you left off.

       << aanndd >>
              Go backward/forward in the playlist.

       EENNTTEERR  Go forward in the playlist.

       SShhiifftt++HHOOMMEE aanndd SShhiifftt++EENNDD
              Go to the first/last playlist entry.

       pp aanndd SSPPAACCEE
              Pause (pressing again unpauses).

       ..      Step forward. Pressing once will pause, every consecutive press
              will play one frame and then go into pause mode again.

       ,,      Step backward. Pressing once will pause, every consecutive press
              will play one frame in reverse and then go into pause mode
              again.

       qq      Stop playing and quit.

       QQ      Like qq, but store the current playback position. Playing the
              same file later will resume at the old playback position if
              possible. See RESUMING PLAYBACK.

       // aanndd **
              Decrease/increase volume.

       KKPP__DDIIVVIIDDEE aanndd KKPP__MMUULLTTIIPPLLYY
              Decrease/increase volume.

       99 aanndd 00
              Decrease/increase volume.

       mm      Mute sound.

       __      Cycle through the available video tracks.

       ##      Cycle through the available audio tracks.

       EE      Cycle through the available Editions.

       ff      Toggle fullscreen (see also ----ffss).

       EESSCC    Exit fullscreen mode.

       TT      Toggle stay-on-top (see also ----oonnttoopp).

       ww aanndd WW
              Decrease/increase pan-and-scan range. The ee key does the same as
              WW currently, but use is discouraged. See ----ppaannssccaann for more
              information.

       oo aanndd PP
              Show progression bar, elapsed time and total duration on the
              OSD.

       OO      Toggle OSD states between normal and playback time/duration.

       vv      Toggle subtitle visibility.

       jj aanndd JJ
              Cycle through the available subtitles.

       zz aanndd ZZ
              Adjust subtitle delay by -/+ 0.1 seconds. The xx key does the
              same as ZZ currently, but use is discouraged.

       ll      Set/clear A-B loop points. See aabb--lloooopp command for details.

       LL      Toggle infinite looping.

       CCttrrll++++ aanndd CCttrrll++--
              Adjust audio delay (A/V sync) by +/- 0.1 seconds.

       CCttrrll++KKPP__AADDDD aanndd CCttrrll++KKPP__SSUUBBTTRRAACCTT
              Adjust audio delay (A/V sync) by +/- 0.1 seconds.

       GG aanndd FF
              Adjust subtitle font size by +/- 10%.

       uu      Switch between applying only ----ssuubb--aassss--** overrides (default) to
              SSA/ASS subtitles, and overriding them almost completely with
              the normal subtitle style. See ----ssuubb--aassss--oovveerrrriiddee for more info.

       VV      Cycle through which video data gets used for ASS rendering.  See
              ----ssuubb--aassss--uussee--vviiddeeoo--ddaattaa for more info.

       rr aanndd RR
              Move subtitles up/down. The tt key does the same as RR currently,
              but use is discouraged.

       ss      Take a screenshot.

       SS      Take a screenshot, without subtitles. (Whether this works
              depends on VO driver support.)

       CCttrrll++ss Take a screenshot, as the window shows it (with subtitles, OSD,
              and scaled video).

       HHOOMMEE   Seek to the beginning of the file.

       PPGGUUPP aanndd PPGGDDWWNN
              Seek to the beginning of the previous/next chapter. In most
              cases, "previous" will actually go to the beginning of the
              current chapter; see ----cchhaapptteerr--sseeeekk--tthhrreesshhoolldd.

       SShhiifftt++PPGGUUPP aanndd SShhiifftt++PPGGDDWWNN
              Seek backward or forward by 10 minutes. (This used to be mapped
              to PGUP/PGDWN without Shift.)

       bb      Activate/deactivate debanding.

       dd      Cycle the deinterlacing filter.

       AA      Cycle aspect ratio override.

       CCttrrll++hh Toggle hardware video decoding on/off.

       AAlltt++LLEEFFTT,, AAlltt++RRIIGGHHTT,, AAlltt++UUPP,, AAlltt++DDOOWWNN
              Move the video rectangle (panning).

       AAlltt++++ aanndd AAlltt++--
              Change video zoom.

       AAlltt++KKPP__AADDDD aanndd AAlltt++KKPP__SSUUBBTTRRAACCTT
              Change video zoom.

       AAlltt++BBAACCKKSSPPAACCEE
              Reset the pan/zoom settings.

       FF88     Show the playlist and the current position in it.

       FF99     Show the list of audio and subtitle streams.

       CCttrrll++vv Append the file or URL in the clipboard to the playlist. If
              nothing is currently playing, it is played immediately. Only
