       Since mpv 0.40.0, it is possible to configure the commands to run with
       mouse actions on some interface elements, and the default behaviors of
       several elements were changed. If you miss some older behaviors, look
       at eettcc//rreessttoorree--oosscc--bbiinnddiinnggss..ccoonnff in the mpv git repository.

   KKeeyy BBiinnddiinnggss
       These key bindings are active by default if nothing else is already
       bound to these keys. In case of collision, the function needs to be
       bound to a different key. See the Script Commands section.

                          ┌────┬───────────────────────────┐
                          │del │ Cycles visibility between │
                          │    │ never / auto (mouse-move) │
                          │    │ / always                  │
                          └────┴───────────────────────────┘
   CCoonnffiigguurraattiioonn
       This script can be customized through a config file
       ssccrriipptt--ooppttss//oosscc..ccoonnff placed in mpv's user directory and through the
       ----ssccrriipptt--ooppttss command-line option. The configuration syntax is
       described in mp.options functions.

   CCoommmmaanndd--lliinnee SSyynnttaaxx
       To avoid collisions with other scripts, all options need to be prefixed
       with oosscc--.

       Example:

          --script-opts=osc-optionA=value1,osc-optionB=value2

   CCoonnffiigguurraabbllee OOppttiioonnss

       llaayyoouutt Default: bottombar

              The layout for the OSC. Currently available are: box, slimbox,
              bottombar, topbar, slimbottombar and slimtopbar. Default
              pre-0.21.0 was 'box'.

       sseeeekkbbaarrssttyyllee
              Default: bar

              Sets the style of the playback position marker and overall shape
              of the seekbar: bbaarr, ddiiaammoonndd or kknnoobb.

       sseeeekkbbaarrhhaannddlleessiizzee
              Default: 0.6

              Size ratio of the seek handle if sseeeekkbbaarrssttyyllee is set to ddiiaammoonndd
              or kknnoobb. This is relative to the full height of the seekbar.

       sseeeekkbbaarrkkeeyyffrraammeess
              Default: yes

              Controls the mode used to seek when dragging the seekbar. If set
              to yyeess, default seeking mode is used (usually keyframes, but
              player defaults and heuristics can change it to exact). If set
              to nnoo, exact seeking on mouse drags will be used instead.
              Keyframes are preferred, but exact seeks may be useful in cases
              where keyframes cannot be found. Note that using exact seeks can
              potentially make mouse dragging much slower.

       sseeeekkrraannggeessttyyllee
              Default: inverted

              Display seekable ranges on the seekbar. bbaarr shows them on the
              full height of the bar, lliinnee as a thick line and iinnvveerrtteedd as a
              thin line that is inverted over playback position markers. nnoonnee
              will hide them. Additionally, sslliiddeerr will show a permanent
              handle inside the seekbar with cached ranges marked inside. Note
              that these will look differently based on the seekbarstyle
              option. Also, sslliiddeerr does not work with sseeeekkbbaarrssttyyllee set to bbaarr.

       sseeeekkrraannggeesseeppaarraattee
              Default: yes

              Controls whether to show line-style seekable ranges on top of
              the seekbar or separately if sseeeekkbbaarrssttyyllee is set to bbaarr.

       sseeeekkrraannggeeaallpphhaa
              Default: 20

              Alpha of the seekable ranges, 0 (opaque) to 255 (fully
              transparent).

       ssccrroollllccoonnttrroollss
              Default: yes

              By default, going up or down with the mouse wheel can trigger
              certain actions (such as seeking) if the mouse is hovering an
              OSC element.  Set to nnoo to disable any special mouse wheel
              behavior.

       ddeeaaddzzoonneessiizzee
              Default: 0.5

              Size of the deadzone. The deadzone is an area that makes the
              mouse act like leaving the window. Movement there won't make the
              OSC show up and it will hide immediately if the mouse enters it.
              The deadzone starts at the window border opposite to the OSC and
              the size controls how much of the window it will span. Values
              between 0.0 and 1.0, where 0 means the OSC will always popup
              with mouse movement in the window, and 1 means the OSC will only
              show up when the mouse hovers it. Default pre-0.21.0 was 0.

       mmiinnmmoouusseemmoovvee
              Default: 0

              Minimum amount of pixels the mouse has to move between ticks to
              make the OSC show up. Default pre-0.21.0 was 3.

       sshhoowwwwiinnddoowweedd
              Default: yes

              Enable the OSC when windowed

       sshhoowwffuullllssccrreeeenn
              Default: yes

              Enable the OSC when fullscreen

       iiddlleessccrreeeenn
              Default: yes

              Show the mpv logo and message when idle

       ssccaalleewwiinnddoowweedd
              Default: 1.0

              Scale factor of the OSC when windowed.

       ssccaalleeffuullllssccrreeeenn
              Default: 1.0

              Scale factor of the OSC when fullscreen

       vviiddssccaallee
              Default: auto

              Scale the OSC with the video.  nnoo tries to keep the OSC size
              constant as much as the window size allows.  aauuttoo scales the OSC
              with the OSD, which is scaled with the window or kept at a
              constant size, depending on the ----oossdd--ssccaallee--bbyy--wwiinnddooww option.

       vvaalliiggnn Default: 0.8

              Vertical alignment in box and slimbox layouts, -1 (top) to 1
              (bottom).

       hhaalliiggnn Default: 0.0

              Horizontal alignment in box and slimbox layouts, -1 (left) to 1
              (right).

       bbaarrmmaarrggiinn
              Default: 0

              Margin from bottom (bottombar, slimbottombar) or top (topbar,
              slimtopbar), in pixels.

       bbooxxaallpphhaa
              Default: 80

              Alpha of the background box, 0 (opaque) to 255 (fully
              transparent)

       hhiiddeettiimmeeoouutt
              Default: 500

              Duration in ms until the OSC hides if no mouse movement, must
              not be negative

       ffaaddeedduurraattiioonn
              Default: 200

              Duration of fade effects in ms, 0 = no fade.

       ffaaddeeiinn Default: no

              Enable fade-in.

       ttiittllee  Default:
              ${!playlist-count==1:[${playlist-pos-1}/${playlist-count}]
              }${media-title}

              String that supports property expansion that will be displayed
              as OSC title.  ASS tags are escaped and newlines are converted
              to spaces.

       ttoooollttiippbboorrddeerr
              Default: 1

              Size of the tooltip outline when using bottombar or topbar
              layouts

       ttiimmeettoottaall
              Default: no

              Show total time instead of time remaining

       rreemmaaiinniinngg__ppllaayyttiimmee
              Default: yes

              Whether the time-remaining display takes speed into account.
              yyeess - how much playback time remains at the current speed.  nnoo -
              how much video-time remains.

       ttiimmeemmss Default: no

              Display timecodes with milliseconds

       ttccssppaaccee
              Default: 100 (allowed: 50-200)

              Adjust space reserved for timecodes (current time and time
              remaining) in the bboottttoommbbaarr and ttooppbbaarr layouts. The timecode
              width depends on the font, and with some fonts the spacing near
              the timecodes becomes too small.  Use values above 100 to
              increase that spacing, or below 100 to decrease it.

       vviissiibbiilliittyy
              Default: auto (auto hide/show on mouse move)

              Also supports nneevveerr and aallwwaayyss

       vviissiibbiilliittyy__mmooddeess
              Default: never_auto_always

              The list of visibility modes to cycle through when calling the
              osc-visibility cycle script message. Modes are separated by __.

       bbooxxmmaaxxcchhaarrss
              Default: 80

              Max chars for the osc title at the box layout. mpv does not
              measure the text width on screen and so it needs to limit it by
              number of chars. The default is conservative to allow wide fonts
              to be used without overflow.  However, with many common fonts a
              bigger number can be used. YMMV.

       bbooxxvviiddeeoo
              Default: no

              Whether to overlay the osc over the video (nnoo), or to box the
              video within the areas not covered by the osc (yyeess). If this
              option is set, the osc may overwrite the ----vviiddeeoo--mmaarrggiinn--rraattiioo--**
              options, even if the user has set them. (It will not overwrite
              them if all of them are set to default values.) Additionally,
              vviissiibbiilliittyy must be set to aallwwaayyss.  Otherwise, this option does
              nothing.

              Currently, this is supported for the bboottttoommbbaarr, sslliimmbboottttoommbbaarr,
              ttooppbbaarr and sslliimmttooppbbaarr layouts only. The other layouts do not
              change if this option is set. Separately, if window controls are
              present (see below), they will be affected regardless of which
              osc layout is in use.

              The border is static and appears even if the OSC is configured
              to appear only on mouse interaction. If the OSC is invisible,
              the border is simply filled with the background color (black by
              default).

              This currently still makes the OSC overlap with subtitles (if
              the ----ssuubb--uussee--mmaarrggiinnss option is set to yyeess, the default). This
              may be fixed later.

              This does not work correctly with video outputs like ----vvoo==xxvv,
              which render OSD into the unscaled video.

       wwiinnddoowwccoonnttrroollss
              Default: auto (Show window controls if there is no window
              border)

              Whether to show window management controls over the video, and
              if so, which side of the window to place them. This may be
              desirable when the window has no decorations, either because
              they have been explicitly disabled (bboorrddeerr==nnoo) or because the
              current platform doesn't support them (eg: gnome-shell with
              wayland).

              The set of window controls is fixed, offering mmiinniimmiizzee,
              mmaaxxiimmiizzee, and qquuiitt. Not all platforms implement mmiinniimmiizzee and
              mmaaxxiimmiizzee, but qquuiitt will always work.

       wwiinnddoowwccoonnttrroollss__aalliiggnnmmeenntt
              Default: right

              If window controls are shown, indicates which side should they
              be aligned to.

              Supports lleefftt and rriigghhtt which will place the controls on those
              respective sides.

       wwiinnddoowwccoonnttrroollss__ttiittllee
              Default: ${media-title}

              String that supports property expansion that will be displayed
              as the windowcontrols title.  ASS tags are escaped, and newlines
              and trailing slashes are stripped.

       ggrreeeennaannddggrruummppyy
              Default: no

              Set to yyeess to reduce festivity (i.e. disable santa hat in
              December.)

       lliivveemmaarrkkeerrss
              Default: yes

              Update chapter markers positions on duration changes, e.g. live
              streams.  The updates are unoptimized - consider disabling it on
              very low-end systems.

       cchhaapptteerr__ffmmtt
              Default: CChhaapptteerr:: %%ss

              Template for the chapter-name display when hovering the seekbar.
              Use nnoo to disable chapter display on hover. Otherwise it's a lua
              ssttrriinngg..ffoorrmmaatt template and %%ss is replaced with the actual name.

       uunniiccooddeemmiinnuuss
              Default: no

              Use a Unicode minus sign instead of an ASCII hyphen when
              displaying the remaining playback time.

       bbaacckkggrroouunndd__ccoolloorr
              Default: #000000

              Sets the background color of the OSC.

       ttiimmeeccooddee__ccoolloorr
              Default: #FFFFFF

              Sets the color of the timecode and seekbar, of the OSC.

       ttiittllee__ccoolloorr
              Default: #FFFFFF

              Sets the color of the video title. Formatted as #RRGGBB.

       ttiimmee__ppooss__ccoolloorr
              Default: #FFFFFF

              Sets the color of the timecode at hover position in the seekbar.

       ttiimmee__ppooss__oouuttlliinnee__ccoolloorr
              Default: #FFFFFF

              Sets the color of the timecode's outline at hover position in
              the seekbar.  Also affects the timecode in the slimbox layout.

       bbuuttttoonnss__ccoolloorr
              Default: #FFFFFF

              Sets the colors of the big buttons.

       ttoopp__bbuuttttoonnss__ccoolloorr
              Default: #FFFFFF

              Sets the colors of the top buttons.

       ssmmaallll__bbuuttttoonnssLL__ccoolloorr
              Default: #FFFFFF

              Sets the colors of the small buttons on the left in the box
              layout.

       ssmmaallll__bbuuttttoonnssRR__ccoolloorr
              Default: #FFFFFF

              Sets the colors of the small buttons on the right in the box
              layout.

       hheelldd__eelleemmeenntt__ccoolloorr
              Default: #999999

              Sets the colors of the elements that are being pressed or held
              down.

       ttiicckk__ddeellaayy
              Default: 1/60

              Sets the minimum interval between OSC redraws in seconds. This
              can be decreased on fast systems to make OSC rendering smoother.

              Ignored if ttiicckk__ddeellaayy__ffoollllooww__ddiissppllaayy__ffppss is set to yes and the
              VO supports the ddiissppllaayy--ffppss property.

       ttiicckk__ddeellaayy__ffoollllooww__ddiissppllaayy__ffppss
              Default: no

              Use display fps to calculate the interval between OSC redraws.

       The following options configure what commands are run when the buttons
       are clicked. mmbbttnn__mmiidd commands are also triggered with sshhiifftt++mmbbttnn__lleefftt.

